        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "Iowa August 2026 ex parte renewal share forecast"
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The target is Iowa's unadjusted August 2026 reporting-cohort state row, original submission O, in dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c. CMS's coverage-retention table defines the denominator as beneficiaries due for renewal, establishing 100 times Metric 5a1 divided by Metric 5. The ledger does not explicitly name its denominator; this forecast uses that official CMS convention. Every historical rate uses O rows, excluding U rows. Historical percentages are calculated from published counts and rounded to one decimal for display."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "official.lookup",
        "call": "curl -sS https://download.medicaid.gov/data/renewal-dataset-september-2026-release.csv; echo exact Iowa row excerpts and read original-submission ex parte and renewal-due counts.",
        "result": "Fetched O-row ex parte/due counts: 2025-06 24861/50336; 2025-07 25484/56759; 2025-08 31141/61485; 2025-09 33291/65844; 2025-10 34099/60348; 2025-11 31383/55647; 2025-12 25294/42878; 2026-01 40708/55874; 2026-02 30409/56221; 2026-03 26384/44726; 2026-04 33892/58912; 2026-05 27200/47958; 2026-06 29594/50176. These yield the 13 historical percentages shown."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "official.lookup",
        "call": "Open the January 2026 CMS snapshot and find Iowa in its Coverage Retention and Disenrollment Rates by State table: https://www.medicaid.gov/resources-for-states/downloads/eligib-oper-and-enrol-snap-jan2026.pdf.",
        "result": "The original-period table reports Iowa with 55,874 renewals due and 73 percent renewed ex parte, corroborating the CSV's calculated 72.9 percent January rate."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "official.lookup",
        "call": "Open the February 2026 CMS snapshot and find Iowa in its Coverage Retention and Disenrollment Rates by State table: https://www.medicaid.gov/resources-for-states/downloads/eligib-oper-and-enrol-snap-feb2026.pdf.",
        "result": "The original-period table reports Iowa with 56,221 renewals due and 54 percent renewed ex parte, corroborating the CSV's calculated 54.1 percent February rate."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "official.lookup",
        "call": "Open the June 2026 CMS snapshot and find Iowa in its Coverage Retention and Disenrollment Rates by State table: https://www.medicaid.gov/resources-for-states/downloads/eligib-oper-and-enrol-snap-jun2026.pdf.",
        "result": "Iowa has 50,176 renewals due, 81 percent total renewed, 59 percent renewed ex parte and 5 percent pending. The CSV provides the exact ex parte numerator of 29,594, giving 58.980389 percent."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Outside-view base rate: the 12 original monthly rates from July 2025 through June 2026 average 56.430021 percent. The January-June 2026 mean is 59.860328 percent, and the March-June mean is 58.054213 percent. These reference-class levels support a persistence forecast near 59-60 percent before adjustments."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Separate adjustments: level uses June's 58.980389 percent. Momentum receives zero extrapolation because January's 72.856785 percent spike reversed to 54.088330 percent in February. A weak seasonal component adds August 2025 minus June 2025, or 1.258027 percentage points; one annual comparison does not establish stable seasonality. No additional one-off adjustment is applied. Iowa's official community engagement page places new-applicant implementation on December 1, 2026 and current-member renewal implementation from February 2027, so that policy receives zero direct August adjustment."
      },
      {
        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: Use a seasonally adjusted persistence prior anchored on June 2026, with July 2025-June 2026 as the dispersion sample. Point = 58.980389 + (50.648126 - 49.390099) = 60.238416 percent, rounded to 60.2. Momentum, additional one-off and policy adjustments are zero. For the 11 successive changes in unrounded monthly rates, mean change = 1.280162 points and squared deviations sum = 633.579323. sigma = 7.959770 percentage points = sqrt(633.579323/10). The normal-approximation one-month 80 percent half-width is 1.28*sigma = 10.188505 points. Scale by sqrt(2) for the two-month June-to-August horizon, assuming independent monthly innovations: half-width = 14.408722 points. Retain January's spike in dispersion. Bounds = 60.238416 +/- 14.408722 = 45.829694 to 74.647138, rounded to 45.8-74.6 percent."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Upside risk is a cohort with more successful automated eligibility verification. Downside risk is a harder-to-verify cohort, processing disruption or renewals classified as form-based. A major automation or reporting change producing a share above 74.6 percent or below 45.8 percent would land outside the interval. The normal approximation and independent-innovation assumption are uncertain with this small historical sample."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Release-date verification gap: the official CMS snapshot announcement page lists June 2026 released September 25, 2026, May released August 28 and April released July 31. It provides no forward August 2026 announcement confirming December 15. Searches of official CMS and Medicaid sources found no confirming calendar. The required resolutionDate is preserved from the supplied ledger, but it is unverified; this run cannot satisfy the official-schedule validation requirement. No date is inferred from cadence. Resolution remains the first official August O-row publication whenever it occurs."
      },
